  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Value Swap\n\nSwap a value in place with a vertical slide so the layout never shifts.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3.3333 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A value changes at a specific story beat: before/after price, status promotion, a token flip.\n- You control the exact swap times.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Values should cycle continuously as a montage: use card-file-flip.\n- The value is a large number counting up: use rolling-number or number-wheel.\n\nVariables:\n- values (string): Values, default \"Draft, In review, Shipped\"\n- at (string): Swap frames, default \"30, 60\"\n- duration (number, 4-24): Duration, default 10\n- distance (number, 4-32): Distance, default 12\n- direction (enum): Direction, default \"up\"\n- font_size (number, 12-200): Font size, default 40\n- color (color): Color, default \"#f2f2f2\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Value Swap\n\n  Swap a value in place with a vertical slide so the layout never shifts. The source example scene (a status word that goes Draft, In review, Shipped) is built in.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/value-swap/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"value-swap\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3.3333\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"values\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Values\", \"description\": \"Comma-separated values; each swap shows the next one.\", \"default\": \"Draft, In review, Shipped\"},\n    {\"id\": \"at\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Swap frames\", \"description\": \"Comma-separated frame numbers (30 fps) where each swap starts.\", \"default\": \"30, 60\"},\n    {\"id\": \"duration\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Duration\", \"description\": \"Frames each swap takes (30 fps).\", \"default\": 10, \"min\": 4, \"max\": 24, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"distance\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Distance\", \"description\": \"How far the values slide, in pixels.\", \"default\": 12, \"min\": 4, \"max\": 32, \"step\": 2, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"direction\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Direction\", \"description\": \"Slide direction of the outgoing value.\", \"default\": \"up\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"up\", \"label\": \"Up\"}, {\"value\": \"down\", \"label\": \"Down\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Text size in pixels.\", \"default\": 40, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 200, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#f2f2f2\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Value Swap</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@600&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .vs-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif); font-weight: 600; }\n        .vs-slot { position: relative; display: inline-block; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .vs-size { visibility: hidden; }\n        .vs-item { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; white-space: nowrap; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"value-swap\" data-duration=\"3.3333\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"vs-clip\" class=\"vs-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3.3333\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"vs-slot\" class=\"vs-slot\"></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            function fit(el, maxPx, size, ratio) {\n              // Shrink el's font size until its scrollWidth fits ratio of the frame width.\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * (ratio || 0.9));\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) { size = Math.max(10, size * (max / el.scrollWidth)); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function ease(name, a, b, c, d) { return CustomEase.create(name, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\"); }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3.3333\");\n            function ip(t, a, b, from, to, e) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : (t - a) / (b - a);\n              p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p));\n              if (e) p = e(p);\n              return from + (to - from) * p;\n            }\n            function hash01(seed) {\n              var h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) { h ^= seed.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            // Snap a frame number down to a stop-motion pose.\n            function qf(frame, step) { return Math.floor(frame / step + 1e-6) * step; }\n            function kf(t, keys, vals, e) {\n              if (t <= keys[0]) return vals[0];\n              for (var i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) if (t <= keys[i + 1]) return ip(t, keys[i], keys[i + 1], vals[i], vals[i + 1], e);\n              return vals[vals.length - 1];\n            }\n            // Per-frame drawing: a pure function of the timeline time, run from a tween's onUpdate.\n            function tick(draw) {\n              tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(tl.time()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var cubOut = ease(\"cub-out\", 0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n            var cubIn = ease(\"cub-in\", 0.55, 0.055, 0.675, 0.19);\n            var cubInOut = ease(\"cub-io\", 0.645, 0.045, 0.355, 1);\n\n            var slot = document.getElementById(\"vs-slot\");\n            var values = str(vars.values, \"Draft, In review, Shipped\").split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n            var ats = str(vars.at, \"30, 60\").split(\",\").map(Number).filter(Number.isFinite);\n            var dur = num(vars.duration, 10, 4, 24);\n            var dist = num(vars.distance, 12, 4, 32) * (pick(vars.direction, [\"up\", \"down\"], \"up\") === \"down\" ? -1 : 1);\n            slot.style.color = col(vars.color, \"#f2f2f2\");\n            var count = Math.max(1, Math.min(values.length, ats.length + 1));\n            var shown = values.slice(0, count);\n            var sz = document.createElement(\"span\");\n            sz.className = \"vs-size\";\n            sz.textContent = shown.reduce(function (a, b) { return b.length > a.length ? b : a; }, \"\");\n            slot.appendChild(sz);\n            var els = shown.map(function (t, i) {\n              var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              s.id = \"vs-item-\" + i;\n              s.className = \"vs-item\";\n              s.textContent = t;\n              slot.appendChild(s);\n              return s;\n            });\n            fit(slot, 0, num(vars.font_size, 40, 12, 200), 0.9);\n            tick(function (t) {\n              var f = t * 30;\n              els.forEach(function (el, i) {\n                var pIn = i > 0 ? ip(f, ats[i - 1], ats[i - 1] + dur, 0, 1, cubInOut) : 1;\n                var pOut = i < count - 1 ? ip(f, ats[i], ats[i] + dur, 0, 1, cubInOut) : 0;\n                var op = pIn * (1 - pOut);\n                el.style.opacity = op <= 0.001 ? 0 : op;\n                el.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + ((1 - pIn) * dist - pOut * dist) + \"px)\";\n              });\n            });\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3.3333\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"value-swap\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
